  "term": "Y chromosome",
  "definition": "The Y chromosome is a genetic marker with uniparental inheritance that is studied in males. Differences in Y-chromosome markers are used in forensic work and in population research to compare groups, examine migration patterns, and identify regional or social structuring.",
